#
# A deliberately CONCAVE L-shaped bracket, written by hand for this project.
# Not derived from anything in references/.
#
# Cross-section in XY, extruded 0.04 m along Z:
#
#   y=0.10  +--+
#           |  |
#   y=0.03  |  +-----+
#           |        |
#   y=0.00  +--------+
#         x=0  0.03  0.10
#
# The convex hull of this shape fills the notch at (0.03, 0.03), so an asset
# whose collider is `convexHull` collides in space the mesh does not occupy.
# That difference is the point of the fixture.

v 0.00 0.00 0.00
v 0.10 0.00 0.00
v 0.10 0.03 0.00
v 0.03 0.03 0.00
v 0.03 0.10 0.00
v 0.00 0.10 0.00
v 0.00 0.00 0.04
v 0.10 0.00 0.04
v 0.10 0.03 0.04
v 0.03 0.03 0.04
v 0.03 0.10 0.04
v 0.00 0.10 0.04

# bottom cap (winding clockwise seen from below => normal -Z)
f 6 5 4 3 2 1
# top cap (counter-clockwise seen from above => normal +Z)
f 7 8 9 10 11 12

# side walls
f 1 2 8 7
f 2 3 9 8
f 3 4 10 9
f 4 5 11 10
f 5 6 12 11
f 6 1 7 12
